A code block whose body spans lines passes through byte-for-byte at top
level (fmt.code_block_literals "a multi-line body ... passes through
byte-for-byte"): no spacing or `;` is added inside it, and the next
statement formats normally. (Inside a procedure the same literal trips
the range-formatting invariant, reported separately.)
-- input.ssl --
:DECLARE fnMulti, vResult;
fnMulti := {|x|x+
1};
vResult:=Eval(fnMulti,1);
-- format --
:DECLARE fnMulti, vResult;
fnMulti := {|x|x+
1};
vResult := Eval(fnMulti, 1);
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
